      "writtenOn": "2026-06-24T13:20:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reasonable idea, but I\u0027d keep it out of this change.\n\nThis CL is deliberately a **no-op** for existing plugins: same default, same `Main-Class`, same packaging — it only makes the value overridable. Renaming the sentinel would change the `Main-Class` header of every plugin JAR built through the macro — churn across all produced artifacts for no runtime benefit (the value is inert, as noted above). This CL is meant to leave existing plugins\u0027 manifests byte-identical, so I\u0027d keep that out.\n\n`Dummy` is also the established idiom in the tree — `git grep main_class` in `gerrit` shows it in `acceptance/BUILD`, `extensions/BUILD` and `plugins/BUILD` as well as here in `bazlets`. Renaming only this occurrence would diverge from the rest; renaming all of them is a separate, tree-wide cleanup rather than something to fold into a feature change.\n\nHappy to do that rename as an independent follow-up if we want it — ideally across all occurrences so the idiom stays consistent.\n\nMinor: with the new suggested default, main_class is always provided, just defaulted, so a `MainClassNotProvided...` name would itself be a bit inaccurate — it\u0027s \"not overridden\" rather than \"not provided.\"\n\nThe trick is to remember where this name is ever seen by a human: it only surfaces in the JVM\u0027s failure when someone runs `java -jar plugin.jar` on a plugin that wasn\u0027t built for it. The JVM prints the literal class name back:\n\n```\nError: Could not find or load main class \u003cNAME\u003e\nCaused by: java.lang.ClassNotFoundException: \u003cNAME\u003e\n```\n\nAlternative suggestion could be: `NoStandaloneMainClass` or `GerritPluginHasNoMainClass`.\nBut then again: good suggestion, better as its own change.\n\nKeeping this CL as-is.",
